## Lab vs Natural for a Three Stone Asscher Ring

A lab-grown asscher center in a three-stone setting follows the same rules as a natural stone. The Hall of Mirrors effect is identical. The shape harmony requirements are identical.

VS1 clarity minimum applies exactly the same way.

The practical case for lab in a three-stone build: a 1.52ct D-IF lab stone costs roughly the same as a 1ct natural E-VS1. The visual size difference is real in a three-stone setting — the Three-Stone Scale Effect amplifies size, so starting with a larger center pays off in final visual impact.

